title: Seat
---
<<if getBool("teacherDistracted")>>
    What do you want to do with the teacher distracted?
<<else>>
    What do you want to do during class?
<<endif>>

-> \[ACTION\] Pump out a chapel essay for a credit? <<if getBool("teacherDistracted")>>
    <<jump Essay>>
-> \[ACTION\] Pay attention. <<if not getBool("teacherDistracted")>>
    <<jump PayAttention>>
-> \[ACTION\] Cause a distraction. <<if not getBool("teacherDistracted") and getInt("hasPaper") > 0 and not getBool("lukeHasPaper")>>
    <<jump Distraction>>
-> Back
    <<stop>>
===

title: PayAttention
---
<<if getBool("lukeHasPaper") and not getBool("handedPosters")>>
    Prof: Luke! I see you not focused. And you, you were yapping with him earlier. Both of you, out of my class!
    <<gameOver "Game Over! Don't let the professor catch Luke preparing posters!">>
<<endif>>

<<if getBool("handedPosters")>>
    <<setBool "failedPosters" true>>
<<endif>>



You pay attention to the lecture, for about 12 minutes...
<<useAction>>
<<stop>>
===

title: Distraction
---
<<useAction>>

<<if getBool("teacherSeesPlayer")>>
    Prof: Dude... I can see you.
    Prof: Get out of my class.
    <<gameOver "Kicked out of class! The Prof is looking directly at you...">>

<<elseif getInt("hasPaper") == 1>>
    You pull out the normal piece of paper.
    <<ThrowNormalPaper>>
    Prof: Bruh...
    Prof: Get out of my class.
    <<gameOver "Kicked out of class! Distraction by throwing a normal piece of paper was not a smart idea...">>

<<elseif getInt("hasPaper") == 2>>
    You pull out the crumpled paper.
    <<ThrowCrumpledPaper>>
    Prof: WHO THREW THAT?!
    <<PaperDistraction>>
<<endif>>

<<setInt "hasPaper" 0>>
<<stop>>
===

title: Essay
---
<<useAction>>
You write up an essay that instantly gets exchanged for a chapel credit!
That's your first credit gained!
<<GotCredit>>
<<stop>>
===

title: Bench
---
Take a quick rest?
-> \[ACTION\] Yes!
    <<jump Resting>>
-> Nah.
    <<stop>>
===

title: Resting
---
You rest for about 10 minutes. 
<<useAction>>
<<stop>>
===

title: ChapelSeat
---
Sit down for chapel?

-> \[ACTION\] Yes.
    <<jump Chapel>>
-> Not yet.
    <<stop>>
===

title: Chapel
---
<<GotCredit>>
<<useAction>>
You gain a chapel credit for listening!

<<cameraToOpitz>>

Chaplain : Welcome to chapel, everyone!
Chaplain : Blah blah blah...

<<cameraToPlayer>>

You listen until chapel is over and are let out.
From here you decide to go to lunch. 

<<nextPeriod>>
<<changeScene "Lunch">>
<<stop>>
===


title: EnterLunch
---
There's gotta be a way to get a chapel credit here! Maybe I can bargin with someone...
<<stop>>
===

title: Eat
---
<<if $boughtMeal or $gotGregsFood>>
    You: Man, this Cowfila is looking GOOD!

    -> \[ACTION\] Eat the meal.
        <<jump EatingMeal>>
    -> Save it for later.
        <<stop>>
<<else>>
    You: I don't have any food to eat!
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===

title: EatingMeal
---
You eat the Cowfila, it filled you up!
<<setBool "starving" false>>
<<if $gotGregsFood>>
    <<set $gotGregsFood = false>>
<<else>>
    <<set $boughtMeal = false>>
<<endif>>
<<useAction>>
<<stop>>
===

title: PosterLeft
---
<<if getBool("handedPosters")>>
    Do you want to put up a poster?
    -> \[ACTION\] Yes.
        <<useAction>>
        Luke: Just in time! Our advertising is sure to work!
        <<setBool "postersHung" true>>
    -> No.
        <<stop>>
<<else>>
    You have nothing to put up on the wall.
<<endif>>
===

title: PosterRight
---
<<if getBool("handedPosters")>>
    Do you want to put up a poster?
    -> \[ACTION\] Yes.
        <<useAction>>
        Teacher: Why are you hanging up a poster in class? I can clearly see you.
        <<gameOver "Kicked out of class! The Prof is looking direclty at you...">>
    -> No.
        <<stop>>
<<else>>
    You have nothing to put up on the wall.
<<endif>>
===
